{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1000344-beast-and-lunars","id":1000344,"title":"Beast and Lunars","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-08T11:08:04-08:00","id":1000344,"title":"Beast and Lunars","content":"Hey, I haven't got the chance to read CoD's Beast, but I was wondering if Ex3 could draw some inspiration from it.<br /> <br /> If you know more about Beast than me, what do you think?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://fivefoldcomicstance.thecomicseries.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Join the Strife</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/90-gonzo","name":"Gonzo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar90_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"934"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T11:14:56-08:00","id":1000349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gonzo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1000344-beast-and-lunars#post1000344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey, I haven't got the chance to read CoD's Beast, but I was wondering if Ex3 could draw some inspiration from it.<br /> <br /> If you know more about Beast than me, what do you think?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. Please god no. Beast is even worse than silver solars or werewolf expies as inspiration for Lunars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6783-notanautomaton","name":"notanautomaton","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T11:25:07-08:00","id":1000354,"title":"","content":"I don't think there's strong linkage between the concept of Beast and of Lunars at all.<br /> <br /> If one had to connect Beasts to any incarnation of Lunars it'd be a distant association with The Atgent Witches homebrew for 2nd Edition, but that's a pretty loose connection.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T14:23:59-08:00","id":1000433,"title":"","content":"I'm going to pray for this to not go downhill very quickly.<br /> <br /> \u200bTo answer the question: I don't really think so, because Beasts are a kind of literal nightmare monster, flitting around inside of people's dreams to provoke and feed off of their primal fears. I think they could be an inspiration for certain aspects of Fair Folk, but the general concept does not really lead to familiar Lunars, I think. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T15:37:29-08:00","id":1000469,"title":"","content":"I have heard Beast was fairly freaky-deaky in a lot of ways - people have compared it to some of the worst books that came out back under White Wolf. I haven't read it though. But yeah, from what I have heard it's not a very good basis for looking at Lunars. The two may touch on a handful of similar themes here or there but fundamentally they both exist in very different conceptual spaces.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T15:38:35-08:00","id":1000471,"title":"","content":"Beasts are thematically so wide open that one could say that we already got Lunars like them in 2e. Just pick up some Fair Folk Charms related to nightmares, and you're probably a good bit of the way there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T17:26:07-08:00","id":1000541,"title":"","content":"When I first heard about Beast I had notions of the Beast and Hero being a bit like a Lunar and Solar bond pair but locked in an eternal struggle, two gifted individuals who are compelled to seek each other out and start spiraling toward a mad obsession to destroy the other that's fueled by visions from past lives telling them that this is inevitable but can be resisted by a number of things, most notably higher callings that give them an excuse to work together.<br /> <br /> It's not Beast: the Primordial in several critical ways but I want to use it somewhere and odds are that'll be Exalted given Ex3's encouraging attitude towards homebrew splat concepts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T17:24:20-08:00","id":1003156,"title":"","content":"Good things for Ex3 Lunars to take from Beast:<br /> *A &quot;Lair&quot; trait to represent how sicknasty your digs are.<br /> *A power called &quot;BEHOLD MY TRUE FORM&quot;<br /> <br /> ...yeah that's about it. Beast tried to make the titular supernaturals allegories for LGBTQ and other marginalized groups with Heroes standing in for reactionaries and hate groups, and BOY HOWDY did the game's actual text take its subtext in some <i>unfortunate</i> directions.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","name":"Thesaurasaurus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T17:29:40-08:00","id":1003157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thesaurasaurus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1000344-beast-and-lunars?p=1003156#post1003156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*A &quot;Lair&quot; trait to represent how sicknasty your digs are.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI can't recall, is the Beast Lair a literal place, or some kind of psychic domain, or a combination of the two?<br /> <br /> Although either way, I wonder how much having such a lair is exactly fitting to Lunars.<br /> <br /> \u200b(I feel as though we're going to go nowhere if this thread is treated as another place to get in digs at Beast that have nothing whatsoever to do with whether or not they can inspire Lunars.)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T17:33:29-08:00","id":1003159,"title":"","content":"It's a place in the Primordial Dream, and you can enter it in dreams or physically by connecting with a conceptually related spooky place where a Beast caused someone to check for a Breaking Point.<br /> <br /> It is... Sorta, vaguely like a Lunar Charm that involved making a kind of den-portal to Elsewhere.<br /> <br /> I don't think that should return in all honesty. Beast has a lot of interesting powers but I really just can't see a way to put them together with Lunars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T18:00:09-08:00","id":1003171,"title":"","content":"I do think there's something similar in that old idea for an Overdrive Charm to empower Lunars to make a certain location somewhere for them to fortify or trap or otherwise stalk and destroy interlopers, while also having an emphasis on the flexibility that seems as though it's going to be a staple now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T18:41:40-08:00","id":1003190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1000344-beast-and-lunars?p=1003157#post1003157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bI can't recall, is the Beast Lair a literal place, or some kind of psychic domain, or a combination of the two?<br /> <br /> Although either way, I wonder how much having such a lair is exactly fitting to Lunars.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's both. Also I didn't mean Lunars should exactly reproduce the trait from Beast, I mean that if Lunars are supposed to be monsters of legend such the Minotaur or the Hydra, they should probably get the Labyrinth or the Lernaean Swamps to go with it. They shouldn't be <i>tied </i>to these locations by any means, but they should definitely enjoy a home field advantage.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u200b(I feel as though we're going to go nowhere if this thread is treated as another place to get in digs at Beast that have nothing whatsoever to do with whether or not they can inspire Lunars.) </div> </div> </div>I'm not trying to get cheap digs in at Beast. I'm saying that I can see definite thematic parallels between what we've seen of Ex3 Lunars (marginalization, outcasts, rage against the system) and what Beast tried to do, and asking <i>please God don't repeat Beast's fuckups.</i><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","name":"Thesaurasaurus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T20:08:49-08:00","id":1003211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gonzo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1000344-beast-and-lunars#post1000344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey, I haven't got the chance to read CoD's Beast, but I was wondering if Ex3 could draw some inspiration from it.<br /> <br /> If you know more about Beast than me, what do you think?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Eh, not really no. I would say Beasts have more in common with Raksha rather than Lunars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>SWTOR Referal: <a href=\"http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/414-gallus","name":"Gallus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"886"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T01:32:12-08:00","id":1003291,"title":"","content":"I like Beast. There I said it. But no I don't think the theme or mood of Beast is a good fit for the Lunars. Raksha, and other denizens of the Wyld certainly. The only thing I might go with is the territory of the Lunar and the Beast's Lair giving the Lunar certain charms or workings that make the Lunar more or less the master of the land that they claim as home. A Beast in it's Lair is a terrifying thing as it can unleash the full force of it's powers and impose a number of tilt conditions on invaders to the Lair. <br /> For example in Exalted: A Lunar that claims a chain of islands has charms or enacted a working that allows the Lunar to:<br /> Raise rocks to smash the hulls of ships as they enter the only harbor.<br /> Turn the water of the harbor against ships by having the tide shift instantly.<br /> Have the water from the springs turn to blood when invaders drink from them.<br /> Have storms with blasts of lightening and hail rain down on the Invaders. <br /> Distort the distance so that anyone scaling the cliffs of an island find themselves never getting close to the top.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T03:48:29-08:00","id":1003307,"title":"","content":"From what I know of Beast, it does not seem Lunar to me.<br /> <br /> i have thought sometimes, they should look into them as the vasis for some new splat. Or Infernals","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T08:36:25-08:00","id":1003418,"title":"","content":"Beast is much more Raksha than it is Infernal.<br /> <br /> In fact, the less Infernals take from Beast, the happier I am.<br /> <br /> (Primarily because if Infernals should take from any World of Darkness splats, it should be Mages, with their hubris and sense of awestruck wonder as well as their alien otherworlds.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T14:45:59-08:00","id":1003617,"title":"","content":"I agree with the Beast =&gt; Raksha comparisson.<br /> <br /> More specifically, a shaped raksha in Creation \u2014 bound to a humanoid shape, a soul that can only be fully expressed in a half-reality half-dream space, feeding on human souls to survive.<br /> <br /> Lunars are almost diametrically opposed to that, aside from the Beasts of Legend theme \u2014 they're free to truly be anyone and anything they want in a way almost no one else is, to a point where, in 3e, they've even once redefined what it means to be Lunar. Next to that, a Beast's lair is more like a shackle than an expression of power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T18:40:30-08:00","id":1003730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManusDomine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1000344-beast-and-lunars?p=1003418#post1003418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> (Primarily because if Infernals should take from any World of Darkness splats, it should be Mages, with their hubris and sense of awestruck wonder as well as their alien otherworlds.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Those are Sidereals. To the extent that anything resembles Mage in Exalted in any way, of course.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T18:48:06-08:00","id":1003732,"title":"","content":"Well, oWoD Mage was the inspiration for 1e Sidereals, anyway. CoD Mage is pretty different from that, though, and Sidereals have likewise grown and changed.<br /> <br /> (Not saying that I agree that CoD Mages should be inspiration for Infernals, mind, just that CoD Mages don't really have anything in particular to do with Sidereals.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T04:53:13-08:00","id":1003862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1000344-beast-and-lunars?p=1003730#post1003730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Those are Sidereals. To the extent that anything resembles Mage in Exalted in any way, of course.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> CoD Mage has so little to do with Sidereals that it is laughable.<br /> <br /> But I can see that this is mostly personal opinion, so I won't argue for fear of going off-topic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T10:34:26-08:00","id":1004001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManusDomine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1000344-beast-and-lunars?p=1003862#post1003862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> CoD Mage has so little to do with Sidereals that it is laughable.<br /> <br /> But I can see that this is mostly personal opinion, so I won't argue for fear of going off-topic.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was talking about WoD Mage, myself. Perhaps the Getimians are taking the CoD Mage spot?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T10:44:26-08:00","id":1004004,"title":"","content":"Guys, Beasts are supposed to be ancient monsters from old legends.<br /> <br /> They're <i>behemoths.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T13:37:03-08:00","id":1004095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thesaurasaurus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1000344-beast-and-lunars?p=1003190#post1003190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">thematic parallels between what we've seen of Ex3 Lunars (marginalization, outcasts, rage against the system) and what Beast tried to do</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI wonder what is precisely meant by marginalization here.<br /> <br /> \u200bLord knows I went the way of considering Lunars in terms of representatives of the generally oppressed before, but by now I'm thinking that Lunars as individuals are outcast not so much for their origins or associations as the fact that Lunars of the Second Age tend to be scary monsters, which isn't entirely fair, but is also something I can't quite fault.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T14:52:53-08:00","id":1004124,"title":"","content":"I'm seeing a lot of disparagement of Beast, especially in relation to any practical measure it could be used to inform Lunars.<br /> I'm not that well-versed in Beast.<br /> Tell me: was it really that bad?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I used to know things. Forbidden things.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/306-brasstreader","name":"Brasstreader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar306_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T15:00:22-08:00","id":1004127,"title":"","content":"There was... heated debate regarding the first draft. I wouldn't be surprised a lot of detractors have never even read the final product.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T15:06:41-08:00","id":1004130,"title":"","content":"I've gone through the ifnal product a bit. I think it still has a lot of fundemental issues on not being good at utilizing subtext, and that there's a lot of aspects of how they try to make that subtext relate to what a Beast is kind of...prolbematic. I also fundementally find how it goes at being a crossover focused game but then going in a weirdly....WoD-ish take on crossover something I dislike also.<br /> <br /> That's my general summation though. I don't think this thread is meant to be a Beast-bash, but there are folks who do have their criticisms to have against it, even in its final form.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T15:10:38-08:00","id":1004134,"title":"","content":"Personally, I like Beast. I mean, yeah, it's not perfect, but you get to play a fucking dragon. And at the end of the day that's what really matters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T16:15:25-08:00","id":1004152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Brasstreader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1000344-beast-and-lunars?p=1004124#post1004124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tell me: was it really that bad?</div> </div> </div> </div>I've only ever read about Exalted Third Edition on Spacewhatever. Tell me, is it really that bad?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T22:49:29-08:00","id":1004257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1000344-beast-and-lunars?p=1004130#post1004130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've gone through the ifnal product a bit. I think it still has a lot of fundemental issues on not being good at utilizing subtext, and that there's a lot of aspects of how they try to make that subtext relate to what a Beast is kind of...prolbematic. I also fundementally find how it goes at being a crossover focused game but then going in a weirdly....WoD-ish take on crossover something I dislike also.<br /> <br /> That's my general summation though. I don't think this thread is meant to be a Beast-bash, but there are folks who do have their criticisms to have against it, even in its final form.<br /> <br /> And stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> A lot of the posters on the Kickstart campaign were extremely vocal both on the campaign and other on line sites. I liked the fact, at least in the original draft, that you were always a Beast and that the moment of awakening was the death of the human caterpillar and the birth of your true form. Many thought this wasn't a good thing. Meh whatever I'll use it if I want. Other complaints Beast is OP, a starting Beast with careful use of powers can probably kill off anything else in the CoD. The cross-over material isn't great, but it is a nice set of workable rules that allow for a mixed group that doesn't feel forced. I like the game and most of the systems work well. I haven't run a game yet, but one of my players is pushing for Beast to be the next game we play. I would rate the idea behind the game as a solid 8/10, the rules 8/10, and the artwork 10/10.<br /> <br /> I don't generally play CoD lines playing mostly Wod and Exalted. Perhaps this is why I don't mind the cross-over rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T00:51:26-08:00","id":1004287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Brasstreader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1000344-beast-and-lunars?p=1004124#post1004124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm seeing a lot of disparagement of Beast, especially in relation to any practical measure it could be used to inform Lunars.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mostly like Beast, but it takes an approach to its themes that Exalted doesn't want to get involved in. It's not that Beast is bad, it's that it's not hugely compatible because of the major differences in tone between CoD and Exalted.<br /> <br /> It's a bit like asking &quot;hey, Vampires can turn into beasts with Protean, can Lunars take inspiration from Vampires?&quot; It's not that they <i>can't</i>, it's just that they're apples and oranges.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T05:51:18-08:00","id":1004353,"title":"","content":"You were essentially a monstrous thing psychically and physically torturing people for power, and the book looked at the characters as heroes even when all but a handful of examples were honestly horrible people. True most vampires are monstrous but we didn't experience someone getting blood drunk. Examples of Beasts feeding getting punished someone for no obvious reason, having personally precious objects destroyed for no obvious reason, having someone run up to you and hurt you then run away, and having someone abusing their power over you to make you feel powerless.<br /> <br /> Originally if you were fed upon you were more likely to become a Hero, a psychopathic monster that wants nothing more then to kill beasts. The more mentally damaged the individual more likely it was to happen. So the game was you being a bully to people and having them become destroyed as people. Other supernaturals supposedly liked them even ones where it made no sense like Changelings.<br /> <br /> There were a lot of interesting mechanics dealing with varying levels of hunger and the Lair was an awsome idea. I have used them as antagonists in a Hunter game before, they worked well there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/363-muscadomestica","name":"MuscaDomestica","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T06:10:11-08:00","id":1004367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MuscaDomestica</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1000344-beast-and-lunars?p=1004353#post1004353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True most vampires are monstrous but <b>we</b> didn't experience someone getting blood drunk.</div> </div> </div> </div>Speak for yourself, please. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T06:26:11-08:00","id":1004372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MuscaDomestica</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1000344-beast-and-lunars?p=1004353#post1004353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">YExamples of Beasts feeding getting punished someone for no obvious reason, having personally precious objects destroyed for no obvious reason, having someone run up to you and hurt you then run away, and having someone abusing their power over you to make you feel powerless.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've seen this argument a lot, and I've never really understood a) how you got this impression from reading the book, or b) how this is worse than <i>actually eating people. </i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T08:50:19-08:00","id":1004447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1000344-beast-and-lunars?p=1004095#post1004095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bI wonder what is precisely meant by marginalization here.<br /> <br /> \u200bLord knows I went the way of considering Lunars in terms of representatives of the generally oppressed before, but by now I'm thinking that Lunars as individuals are outcast not so much for their origins or associations as the fact that Lunars of the Second Age tend to be scary monsters, which isn't entirely fair, but is also something I can't quite fault.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a world-spanning empire and about half of Heaven itself backing a sophisticated and omnipresent apparatus for hunting them down and murdering them? And unlike Solars, they don't hold the literal Mandate of Heaven, a spiritual blank check to make of the world what they wish, with concrete metaphysical backing? They don't have mystical powers to sway the minds of the masses in the face of overwhelming propaganda, and they can't demand access to the body politic except by eating its heart and impersonating it. They aren't the rightful heirs to the First Age, with all of its wonders and glory - they are, in fact, unique in this: Abyssals and Infernals are part of the same legacy as the Solars, warped or not, while Dragon-Blooded can claim right of conquest and back it up with a nigh-invincible military apparatus and the Sidereals back them up. In the event that a Lunar DOES build something worthwhile, something genuinely <i>theirs</i>, it's likely going to be immediately rolled by the Empire, annexed, and turned against them. Many of the suggestions I've seen (more on this forum than by the devs themselves, mind) for what to do when the Realm comes calling amount to &quot;turn into a bird and flee.&quot; The Silver Pact's main strategy to counter this is a long, gruesome war of attrition; we'll have to wait for the DB and Lunar hardbacks to see if it's actually accomplished anything except for making Creation measurably worse.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1000344-beast-and-lunars?p=1004372#post1004372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've seen this argument a lot, and I've never really understood a) how you got this impression from reading the book, or b) how this is worse than <i>actually eating people.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>The examples are very much there, and pretending they aren't is disingenuous. As for how it's worse, the problem is twofold: First, Vampire is meant as a metaphor for a variety of dysfunctional or abusive relationships, and the blood-drinking (which, importantly, <i>need not be fatal</i>) exists as a filter of the fantastical so that players aren't necessarily engaging directly with the full ugliness of the real-life situations for which it is an allegory. Nobody has to worry about triggering another player's PTSD with Ghouls or Frenzy mechanics or the Presence Discipline, <i>even though these are all meant to reference controlling abuse and domestic violence</i>. Yes, Elizabeth Bathory was real, but such a freakish one-off that it's <i>staggeringly</i>-unlikely any player at your table will break down sobbing because of Clan Ventrue.<br /> <br /> Beast doesn't have this filter. Beasts, more often than not, feed by abusing people, and they abuse people by <i>actually abusing them</i>. Vandalism, threatening messages, gaslighting, leveraging a position of authority to terrorize one's subordinates, and murder. Even their murders are more fucked-up than a vampire's killings - more often than not, a vampire lost control of their thirst and is rightly-horrified of what they've done, and if they're not, it's a sign that they're slipping toward BAD END. It evokes the horror and shame of having done something terrible and wrong in the heat of passion, and the fundamental tragedy of vampiric existence. When a Beast kills, it's to satisfy a deep, psychological need by reinforcing an internal narrative and asserting their primacy over the bulk of humanity. Their idealized relationship with Heroes isn't one of deadly antagonism, but of the Beast asserting the Hero's fundamental irrelevance by putting the Hero in their place. That necessary curtain of metaphor collapses here because the Beast's violence doesn't feel very metaphorical at all. I'm not exaggerating when I say that it reads like a serial killer's manifesto.<br /> <br /> This segues into the second big issue with Beast that the rest of the WoD/CoD gamelines don't have: It tries very hard to <i>justify</i> its protagonists' monstrosity. The Sabbat belief that humans should be cattle for their vampire overlords is why the Sabbat are the bad guys, <i>even to other vampires</i>. Werewolves are fundamentally-inhuman in mindset, and large portions of the book are given over to characters who REMEMBER what it was to feel human coming to terms with an unavoidable need to hunt and kill other sapient beings (they also have the Ghost Wolves to act as an audience surrogate, taking a look at Werewolf 'society' and asking &quot;what even the sweet crispy fuck?&quot;) Slashers are <i>slashers</i>, meant first and foremost as an antagonist splat, and when they aren't they're for playing games in the vein of <i>Suicide Squad</i>. Beast asks the Hunters and Heroes, &quot;What gives you the <i>right </i>to hunt me?&quot; and then turns a deaf ear to the answer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","name":"Thesaurasaurus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T09:24:35-08:00","id":1004467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thesaurasaurus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1000344-beast-and-lunars?p=1004447#post1004447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This segues into the second big issue with Beast that the rest of the WoD/CoD gamelines don't have: It tries very hard to <i>justify</i> its protagonists' monstrosity.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it doesn't. The <i>beasts themselves</i> do that. The whole &quot;lessons&quot; thing is something they try to do to give something back to the people they feed on (which they have to do because if they don't they eventually <i>die</i>) and there's an entire sidebar noting that it's essentially a load of bullshit they came up with to help themselves sleep at night. <br /> <br /> The vast majority of player beasts are expected to try and restrict their feeding to the bastards who actually <i>deserve</i> it. The examples can come across as a bit nastier because beasts (non-nemesis ones, at least) don't <i>have</i> to do that and they were trying to be generic. <br /> <br /> And also the first example, &quot;<span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><i>punished someone for no obvious reason</i></span></span></span><i>&quot; </i>is in fact <i>not</i> in the book at all, because Nemesis' need their victims to <i>know</i> why they're being punished or it doesn't work. And the rest are gross oversimplifications. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T10:05:53-08:00","id":1004497,"title":"","content":"So here's my main issue with Beast:<br /> <br /> Beasts, by their natures, hurt people. They are dangerous to be around, feed on others for sustenance and can't stop doing that. And as note,d the original write-up, their presence encouraged Heroism. So in the end, a beast is a parasite that hurts people. Like a vampire in a sense.<br /> <br /> It's just that a vampire doesn't go and then claims it's the victim here. I think to me that's the fundemental disconnect I have with Beast. I think to me that's the big issue I feel of it. It has this weird situation-blindness where that the world hates you for being a monstrous predator is somehow the world's fault. And it's done I think with a goal to be contrarian to other CoD games (which feels almost ham-fisted since they feel more honest), with a crossover angle to them somehow (which I fail to see hwo it fits for Changelings who try to escape absue, magi who generally are just human not monsters and Created with lines that seem to be encouraging going Centimanus).<br /> <br /> I also feel Heroes didn't help this. In the orignal write-up, a Hero while usually someone prone to it, is made that by the Beast. Yet it's somehwo the Hero's fault for playing into what the Beast made them.<br /> <br /> And this is all in a context of trying to sell Beasts as a representative of LGBTQ people through metaphor. But I think it does it without first questioning what a beast <i>is</i> first. Since it in a way to me feels like it's just by accident stumbling into being exactly what folks say about LGBTQ people (that they are harmful to themselves and others and don't care). To me at least, it is both odd in its messaging and through that, undermines and actively harms its own message.<br /> <br /> It's a game that wants to be about lashing-out agasint abusers. But to me reads about abusers blaming their victims. And while some supernaturals kind of do that (some Kindred more or less go this route), the game doesn't really praise them for it but often narratively feels liek it more calls them out on that.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T10:06:47-08:00","id":1004498,"title":"","content":"Which, I guess I should add, means that the pscyhological torture and alien horror stuff? Probably more Fair Folk than Lunar, who are much more about primal violence, god-bodies and blood I feel.<br /> <br /> And stuff.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T10:42:07-08:00","id":1004520,"title":"","content":"Beasts gain power by, and this is an actual example from the book, beating up a teenager who steals someone's Halloween candy, kidnapping them, and then force feeding them poisoned candy until they die, to teach them a lesson. Beast in general is all about giving back 20x what was given to horrifying ends.<br /> <br /> The only change with the above example from the draft that people hated to the release version? The draft had you doing that to a kid who was stealing kids candy, not a teenager.<br /> <br /> This is all tied to how Beasts are supposed to represent LGBTQ people, and Heroes as Republican/anti gay people. But in a world where LGBTQ people are literally ripping someone apart for punching someone else in the face, it's hard to really hate the Heroes who put them down, even if they're jerks. So it's just a super offensive metaphor, especially to people like me who are part of the LGBTQ groupings.<br /> <br /> If you can't see how that's more fucked up than vampires drinking blood (which is not fatal in 99% of cases) then uh... Yeah.<br /> <br /> Beast is a bad game, and no one sane should like it unless they also liked playing Abyssals using dead baby cannons and etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11919-kittyempress","name":"KittyEmpress","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11919_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"142"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T10:46:47-08:00","id":1004523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KittyEmpress</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1000344-beast-and-lunars?p=1004520#post1004520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beasts gain power by, and this is an actual example from the book, beating up a teenager who steals someone's Halloween candy, kidnapping them, and then force feeding them poisoned candy until they die, to teach them a lesson.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good fucking god, that's not even CLOSE to how that example went.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 11-17-2016, 01:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T11:19:44-08:00","id":1004538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1000344-beast-and-lunars?p=1004523#post1004523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Good fucking god, that's not even CLOSE to how that example went.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11919-kittyempress\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11919_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11919\" data-vbnamecard=\"11919\">KittyEmpress</a>, Old Lady Winters didn't force-feed the kid poisoned candy until he died, she just gave him a single dose, followed him home, terrorized him in his bedroom (including by smothering him with a plastic bag until he vomited) and then left him ALIVE. With his bedroom turned into an extension of her personal nightmare dimension, so Winters could drop in to feed on him again whenever she's peckish. Get it right, GOD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","name":"Thesaurasaurus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T11:30:47-08:00","id":1004546,"title":"","content":"That's not actually entirely right either. She didn't follow him home. She broke in, poisoned the candy <i>that he stole </i>and then waited until he started retching. Then smothered him a bit with a plastic Halloween bag <i>that he also stole</i> and dropped a line about not disrespecting holidays belonging to monsters.<br /> <br /> Also the victim here was a <i>frat boy. </i>Y'know, in university? He's a grown man stealing stuff from kids that she had <i>sworn to protect</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":".  typo 11-17-2016, 04:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T11:34:00-08:00","id":1004551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1000344-beast-and-lunars?p=1000433#post1000433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm going to pray for this to not go downhill very quickly.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Glob, why don't you ever answer me?!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T14:37:19-08:00","id":1004638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1000344-beast-and-lunars?p=1004127#post1004127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There was... heated debate regarding the first draft. I wouldn't be surprised a lot of detractors have never even read the final product.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Most of us have, we just still don't like the final product.<br /> <br /> I'm super hyped for Deviant though.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1000344-beast-and-lunars?p=1004001#post1004001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was talking about WoD Mage, myself. Perhaps the Getimians are taking the CoD Mage spot?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a good point actually.<br /> <br /> Damn you, now I have <i>hopes and dreams that can be shattered against the harsh reality</i>.<br /> <br /> Why would you do this to me?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T14:49:09-08:00","id":1004648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManusDomine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1000344-beast-and-lunars?p=1004638#post1004638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's a good point actually.<br /> <br /> Damn you, now I have <i>hopes and dreams that can be shattered against the harsh reality</i>.<br /> <br /> Why would you do this to me?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because you're a M:tAs fan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T14:55:07-08:00","id":1004654,"title":"","content":"Ok, I've been thinking and I think I came up with an unambiguously heroic, non-abusive Beast:<br /> <br /> A Collector who sates their hunger by hunting down rapists and cutting their dicks off. They collect Rapist Dicks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T15:27:48-08:00","id":1004675,"title":"","content":"So the solution to violent and sadistic acts is more violence and sadism. I think this kind of show